; A program with no C library under it. There is no `std:io` here and nothing
; to print with, so the answer leaves through the exit status, which is what
; `boot/start.s` does with what `main` returns.
;
; The arithmetic is deliberately v0.8's: a hexadecimal literal and a `bit-and`,
; which is the vocabulary a driver is written in and did not exist before
; v0.8.0.

(fn masked ((value i64)) -> i64
  (bit-and value 0xFF))

(fn main () -> i64
  (masked 1322))
